{"ts":"2026-08-03T06:21:42.773Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_instance":"f776625cfc2dc9d344e5cac5","agent_provenance":{"model":null,"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"1","source":"environment"},"topic":null},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-eq9dlw"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"The session-role dimension is wired to a boolean child-session flag, so every nested claude-code invocation records the role literally as \"1\" and fleet analytics will group real work under a meaningless label"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Measured on 2026-08-03 against pm 2026.8.3.\n\nThe claude-code harness descriptor in src/core/shared/author.ts declares provenance_environment_keys.role = ['CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION']. That variable is a boolean marker meaning 'this invocation is a nested session'; its value in a live session is the literal string '1'. The resolver treats any non-blank value as the role observation, so a fresh mutation on 2026-08-03 records agent_provenance.role = {value: '1', source: 'environment'}.\n\nThis reads as legitimate provenance. The source is 'environment', which is the same source category a genuinely declared role would carry, so no consumer can distinguish a real role from this artifact by inspecting the entry. Fleet attribution analytics group by role; a permanently immutable population of entries labelled role '1' is worse than a population labelled null, because null is honest about absence and '1' is not.\n\nThe wiring appears to be a category error introduced while closing the gap that role had no descriptor key on any harness. Filling the slot with the only role-adjacent variable the harness exports satisfies a coverage metric while defeating the purpose of the dimension. If the nested-session fact is worth recording it deserves its own dimension with its own name and a boolean value domain.\n\nRelated but distinct: whether a declared resolver that fails is distinguishable from a dimension a harness cannot supply is its own finding. This one is the inverse - a resolver that succeeds and records a value that means nothing.\n\nScope is the role dimension wiring and the general rule that a descriptor key must match the value domain of the dimension it feeds."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:sdk","data-quality","identity","provenance"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-08-03T06:21:42.773Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-08-03T06:21:42.773Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"No provenance dimension is sourced from an environment key whose value domain is boolean or presence-only; Each descriptor key declares the dimension value domain it is expected to carry, and a value outside that domain is refused rather than recorded; The nested-session fact, if worth recording, is recorded in a dimension whose name says what it means rather than being smuggled into role; A corpus check reports zero provenance values that are bare booleans or single digits across all dimensions"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-5oj5"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/severity","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/environment","value":"pm 2026.8.3, claude-code harness with CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION=1, Linux"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/repro_steps","value":"Run a pm mutation from a nested/child claude-code session and read agent_provenance.role on the newest history entry."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"role is either a descriptive session role the operator declared, or null when the harness publishes no role."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"role is {value: \"1\", source: \"environment\"}. The claude-code descriptor maps the role dimension to CLAUDE_CODE_CHILD_SESSION, which is a presence/boolean flag whose value is the string \"1\", not a role name."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/component","value":"core/shared/author"}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"d8cf91aaf3925f7986751df37d377c67cf33a3dcdd10aa289038e245ab2e4923","message":""}
